cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tutorial, please cite it as below."
title: "How to Choose Your Statistical Test Before You Run It: A Decision-Based Guide to Statistical Analysis in Aquatic Sciences for Young Scientists"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible R tutorial that walks through the full cycle of environmental
  data analysis in aquatic sciences: formulating a structured research question,
  stating an a priori hypothesis, diagnosing and cleaning a messy dataset, and
  choosing a statistical test from the study design rather than from the results.
  Companion material to an article submitted to Limnology and Oceanography Bulletin.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rodrigues da Conceicao"
    given-names: "Juline"
  - family-names: "Zorzal-Almeida"
    given-names: "Stefano"
keywords:
  - reproducible research
  - statistics
  - aquatic sciences
  - data cleaning
  - R
  - confirmatory analysis
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/julinerodrigues/before-you-run-the-test"
